Rewritten for Nodecode: the provider profile its Hermes plugin registers --
the id and display name, the base URL https://aistupidlevel.info/v1 and its
OpenAI chat wire, the router key variable ASL_ROUTER_KEY, the signup page,
the routing modes it lists as fallback models, and the fast near-top mode it
names for titles and compression. They are a catalog row here rather than an
in-process provider object, so the model picker and the listing read them the
way they read any provider's. Left out: the profile fields that mean nothing
outside the Hermes registry (its aliases, its api_mode, supports_vision, and
the base-URL environment variable, which is the section's base_url here), and
the original's defensive drop of profile fields an older Hermes build lacks,
since a Nodecode catalog row carries no such version skew.
